       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose per administration:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Total daily dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatient use is 3,200 mg/day, and the usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens would be:\n- 400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily, not to exceed 3,200 mg/day. For example, 800 mg PO TID is 2,400 mg/day.\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours, which is 1,600 mg/day. This was possibly the intended total.\n\nDid you mean a total of 1,600 mg/day, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or did you mean a different dose or frequency? Once you confirm, I'll enter the order. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that explicitly and I can add a note documenting the override."
